<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<chapter xml:id="ch12-chapter-ht-compare-means" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Comparing Groups - Quantitative Response</title>

  <introduction>
    <p> In this chapter students learn how to test whether an association is statistically discernible. The focus will be on comparing two groups when then the response variable is quantitative. Students will perform randomization tests for comparing population means. 
      We begin with a comparison of two groups and extend this to any number of groups. 
      We also look at the special case of paired data. 
    </p>
  </introduction>



  <objectives>
    <ol>
    <li>Explore...</li>

    <li>Learn...</li>

    <li>Understand...</li>

    <li>Apply...</li>
  </ol>
  </objectives>



  

